@section Running this book

This section covers the pinned toolchain, the @command{just} recipes, the
layout of @file{examples/}, @file{exercises/}, and @file{solutions/}, and how
a test proves an exercise. Running the code is optional: every result a
listing displays is also written in the listing as a comment, so the book
reads standalone in print, HTML, and EPUB alike.

@heading The toolchain

The TypeScript edition is a pnpm workspace. The pins live once in
@file{typescript/package.json}, and every chapter package builds against
them:

@multitable @columnfractions .50 .45
@item Node, pinned by @file{.node-version} @tab 24.21.0
@item pnpm @tab 12.5.1
@item TypeScript @tab 7.0.2
@item vitest @tab 5.0.1
@item fast-check @tab 4.10.2
@item Biome, formatter and linter @tab 2.5.14
@item Effect and @@effect/vitest @tab 4.0.0-rc.117
@end multitable

@noindent
The compiler settings are house rules, not suggestions.
@file{tsconfig.base.json} turns on @code{strict} and keeps it company:
@code{noUncheckedIndexedAccess} makes every index read a possibility of
nothing, @code{exactOptionalPropertyTypes} keeps ``absent'' and
``undefined'' distinct, and @code{verbatimModuleSyntax} keeps the type and
value worlds apart at import time. Two prohibitions the settings cannot
express are enforced in review: no @code{any}, and no non-null assertion.
Biome owns formatting and linting in one pass, so a listing in this book is
formatted the way @command{biome check} would leave it.

@heading The layout

The @file{typescript/} tree holds six chapter packages, @code{ch0} through
@code{ch5}, under @file{packages/}. Each is a workspace package named
@code{@@sicp-ts/ch@var{N}}, whose @file{src/} carries the book listings,
numbered in section order, one file per section. Three directories at the
workspace root carry the code the reader writes, and every chapter package
compiles and tests them beside its own sources:

@multitable @columnfractions .38 .57
@item Directory @tab Contents
@item @file{typescript/examples/ch@var{N}/} @tab runnable demos beyond the listings, one file each, tested
@item @file{typescript/exercises/ch@var{N}/} @tab one scaffold per exercise, @file{ex_N_MM.ts}, statement as a doc comment
@item @file{typescript/solutions/ch@var{N}/} @tab the same file names as @file{exercises/}, solved, tested, with a rationale @file{ex_N_MM.md}
@end multitable

@noindent
Chapter 0 itself is the primer you are reading; its package carries the
sections' listings in @file{packages/ch0/src/}, and @ref{0.2} through
@ref{0.8} use them as they teach.

@heading The recipes

The @command{just} recipes wrap the commands worth remembering:

@example
just setup      # mise install, corepack enable,
                # pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
just fmt        # pnpm biome format .
just lint       # pnpm biome check . + tsc --noEmit
                # in every chapter package
just test       # pnpm vitest run
just scaffold   # pnpm vitest run --reporter=verbose
                # pending report: todo lines only
@end example

@noindent
@command{just lint} is the gate: it fixes nothing, checks formatting,
applies the linter, and type-checks all six chapter packages under the
strict settings. A scaffold that is still pending does not break it, which
is what @code{PendingSolution} is for (@ref{0.7}).

@heading How a test proves an exercise

Every exercise in this book carries three artifacts. The statement lives in
the section text. The scaffold lives in @file{exercises/}: a function body
that throws @code{PendingSolution} and a @code{test.todo} carrying the
exercise's name, so the scaffold compiles and the gate stays green while it
is unsolved. The solution lives in @file{solutions/} under the same name: a
real implementation whose test asserts exactly the values the book's
statement leads to, with a short rationale beside it. A listing file proves
itself the same way, which the shortest example in the book shows in full:

@example typescript
export const square = (x: number): number => x * x;
@end example

@noindent
The definition is the listing; the test is the proof. The file is
@file{packages/ch0/src/01-running-this-book.ts}, and its call reads
@code{square(21)} with the result written beside it:

@example typescript
square(21)
// => 441
@end example

@noindent
That comment shape is the book's interaction convention, introduced for
real in @ref{0.2} and specified in @ref{0.8}.

